# REST Client tests for review-service. Copy results into docs/api-test-plan.md (ID, request, expected, actual, pass/fail).
# Tokens: paste the output of bash platform/get-token.sh reviewer2 / student / admin below while testing (they last
# 1 hour). Don't commit them. Set baseUrl from: source platform/vars.sh && echo $API_URL
# Replace APP_ID with an applicationId from the queue (T-REV-03).
@baseUrl = http://REPLACE_API_ID.execute-api.localhost.floci.io:4566
@reviewer = PASTE_REVIEWER_TOKEN
@student = PASTE_STUDENT_TOKEN
@admin = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN
@appId = APP_ID

### T-REV-01 queue without a token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/queue

### T-REV-02 queue as a student -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{student}}

### T-REV-03 queue as a reviewer -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}

### T-REV-04 claim with the wrong Content-Type -> 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Content-Type: text/plain

applicationId={{appId}}

### T-REV-05 claim with an invalid id -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "applicationId": "../x" }

### T-REV-06 claim an unknown id -> 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "applicationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000" }

### T-REV-07 claim -> 201 (reviewerId in the body is ignored)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "applicationId": "{{appId}}", "reviewerId": "someone-else" }

### T-REV-07b claim the same one again -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "applicationId": "{{appId}}" }

### my claims and reviews -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}

### open the claimed application + rubric -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{appId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}

### T-REV-19 PDF link (5 minutes) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{appId}}/pdf
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}

### T-REV-11 score out of range -> 400 (use the rubric's criterionIds)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{appId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "scores": { "academic": 11, "essay": 7, "need": 5 } }

### T-REV-12 score -> 200, server total (totalScore in the body is ignored)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{appId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "scores": { "academic": 8, "essay": 7, "need": 5 }, "totalScore": 100, "comment": "Strong essay" }

### T-REV-13 score again -> 409 (final)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{appId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "scores": { "academic": 10, "essay": 10, "need": 10 } }

### T-REV-15 flag (on a different claimed application) -> 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{appId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "flagged": true, "flagReason": "ineligible", "flagNote": "GPA in the PDF is 2.1" }

### T-REV-16 release my claim -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{appId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}

### T-REV-17 admin releases any claim -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{appId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### T-REV-18 student tries to release -> 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{appId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{student}}

### T-REV-22 foreign origin -> no Access-Control-Allow-Origin in the response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewer}}
Origin: http://evil.example

### T-REV-20 (CLI, not HTTP) expiry job
# Put an under_review application with claimedAt older than 48 hours in Applications (test data), then:
# aws lambda invoke --function-name release-expired-claims out.json && cat out.json
# Expected: {"checked":1,"released":1}, the application is back to submitted, claim_expired in AuditLog.
